    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "fact": "The statutory text of the Dodd-Frank Act defines a 'whistleblower' in 15 U.S.C. § 78u-6(a)(6) as 'any individual who provides, in accordance with the rules and regulations of the Commission, information to the Commission.'",
      "source_date": "2010-07-21"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "fact": "In United States v. X-Citement Video, Inc. (1994), the Supreme Court held that where statutory text is clear and unambiguous, the Court must give effect to the plain meaning of the words without resorting to legislative history or policy arguments.",
      "source_date": "1994-06-22"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "fact": "In Chevron U.S.A. Inc. v. Natural Resources Defense Council, Inc. (1984), the Court established that if a statute is ambiguous, courts must defer to the agency's reasonable interpretation, but if the statute is clear, the agency's interpretation is not controlling.",
