    {
      "id": 3,
      "fact": "In Fisher v. University of Texas (Fisher I) (2013), the Supreme Court vacated the Fifth Circuit's judgment and remanded the case, holding that the lower court had applied the wrong standard of review by giving too much deference to the university's assertion that its race-conscious admissions program was necessary, and reaffirmed that strict scrutiny must be applied in all cases involving racial classifications.",
